{
  "note": "Four roots, each its own census page, both sides for both themes, on the mirror (http://localhost:4184/geist/command-menu) and the census page of the docs (http://localhost:4180/census/command-menu), the pane at 1100 by 900. The page's three examples render the closed opener on both sides (no root); the eight sketches that follow render the open states: the docs page's census-only examples carry their markup closed (ids `sk-*`), and the `prepare` step opens them and types the two queries before the read (inject census.js into the docs tab first: a script tag for http://localhost:4183/census.js). The dialog run reads the native dialog with its backdrop (the reference's overlay, a sibling) and the input block, list and empty message inside it; the item, group and divider runs read every shown row, group and divider through `each` (a hidden one is left out on both sides, as the reference unmounts a row that scores 0). Soft by declaration: the searchbox's width follows the Esc chip's text; the chip, the label, the sr title and description, the empty message and its query follow the text; the keys box and the suffix sit behind an auto margin the label's width decides. Last run: 0 hard on all eight pages.",
  "themes": ["light", "dark"],
